    "text": "Summary"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000011",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0020-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0021-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0021-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0022-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0022-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0023-l0000"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0020-l0001",
      "p0001-n0021-l0000",
      "p0001-n0022-l0000",
      "p0001-n0023-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Our planet is getting thirstier and thirstier. Water scarcity has become an increasingly hard but urgent problem. To make contributions to solve the water problems, we proposed a metric model to identify the ability of each country to manage water scarcity, and offered solutions to a country considered water over-loaded."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000012",
    "issues": [
      "private_use_glyph_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0024-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0025-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0025-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0026-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0026-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0027-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0027-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0028-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0028-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0029-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0029-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0030-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0030-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0031-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0031-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0032-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0032-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0033-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0033-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0034-l0000"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0024-l0000",
      "p0001-n0025-l0000",
      "p0001-n0026-l0000",
      "p0001-n0027-l0000",
      "p0001-n0028-l0000",
      "p0001-n0029-l0000",
      "p0001-n0030-l0000",
      "p0001-n0031-l0000",
      "p0001-n0032-l0000",
      "p0001-n0033-l0000",
      "p0001-n0034-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "First we developed our metric, Total Scarcity Metric, and divided it into Physical Scarcity Metric (affected by environmental factors and population) and Economic Scarcity Metric (affected by social factors other than population) by the two causes of water scarcity. The detailed factors were selected to make a difference. We made some adjustments to an indicator we found widely-used in the literatures, and determine Physical Scarcity Metric based on it. For Economic Scarcity Metric, we built a factor model with its weight calculated by Grey Relational Analysis. To combine them, we introduced a parameter \uf061 revealing the relative emphasis between physical scarcity and economic scarcity of each country. Its value varies by countries, so it\u2019s more proper to discuss it in the country level. Then we used data from 83 countries to verify our model, and found a similar water scarcity distribution compared to UN\u2019s \u201cWorld Scarcity Map\u201d. By providing sensitivity analysis on\uf061,we indicated the importance of its selection for each country."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000013",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0035-l0000",
